\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \{\uc0\u8232 "question_id": "Q01",\u8232 "marks": [\u8232 \{\u8232 "no": 1,\u8232 "mark": "Partly",\u8232 "evidence": "the police officer should be slow in recording an FIR and he should record an FIR only if he finds a prima facie case.",\u8232 "reason": "It concerns 498A complaints and police caution, but addresses FIR registration rather than whether registration automatically permits arrest.",\u8232 "confidence": "high"\u8232 \},\u8232 \{\u8232 "no": 2,\u8232 "mark": "Yes",\u8232 "evidence": "It is not correct to say that just because FIR is registered, the accused person can be arrested immediately.",\u8232 "reason": "It directly states that FIR registration alone does not justify immediate arrest and that arrest requires separate justification.",\u8232 "confidence": "high"\u8232 \},\u8232 \{\u8232 "no": 3,\u8232 "mark": "No",\u8232 "evidence": "since the appellant has been in Gulf, arrest could not be made and therefore police requested the court to issue a warrant of arrest",\u8232 "reason": "It describes one accused's circumstances and a warrant request rather than stating the rule governing automatic arrest after 498A registration.",\u8232 "confidence": "high"\u8232 \},\u8232 \{\u8232 "no": 4,\u8232 "mark": "Partly",\u8232 "evidence": "The need for caution in exercising the drastic power of arrest has been emphasized time and again by Courts",\u8232 "reason": "It supports caution in 498A arrests but does not itself state that registration cannot automatically trigger arrest.",\u8232 "confidence": "high"\u8232 \},\u8232 \{\u8232 "no": 5,\u8232 "mark": "Partly",\u8232 "evidence": "the arrest be made, only after following the restrictions imposed under Section 41(b).",\u8232 "reason": "It gives general Section 41 arrest safeguards but concerns other offences rather than specifically addressing automatic arrest after 498A registration.",\u8232 "confidence": "medium"\u8232 \},\u8232 \{\u8232 "no": 6,\u8232 "mark": "Yes",\u8232 "evidence": "he is not expected to act in a mechanical manner and in all cases to arrest the accused as soon as the report is lodged.",\u8232 "reason": "It directly rejects mechanical arrest immediately after a report and explains that arrest is discretionary and must be cautiously exercised.",\u8232 "confidence": "high"\u8232 \},\u8232 \{\u8232 "no": 7,\u8232 "mark": "Yes",\u8232 "evidence": "he is not expected to act in a mechanical manner and in all cases to arrest the accused as soon as the report is lodged.",\u8232 "reason": "It directly states that police need not automatically arrest after a report and that arrest must be exercised cautiously.",\u8232 "confidence": "high"\u8232 \},\u8232 \{\u8232 "no": 8,\u8232 "mark": "Yes",\u8232 "evidence": "arrest of the accused immediately on registration of FIR is not at all mandatory.",\u8232 "reason": "It directly distinguishes FIR registration from arrest and expressly says immediate arrest after registration is not mandatory.",\u8232 "confidence": "high"\u8232 \},\u8232 \{\u8232 "no": 9,\u8232 "mark": "Partly",\u8232 "evidence": "Section 41A Cr.PC aimed to avoid unnecessary arrest or threat of arrest looming large on accused requires to be vitalised.",\u8232 "reason": "It explains a safeguard against unnecessary arrest but does not expressly address automatic arrest following 498A registration.",\u8232 "confidence": "high"\u8232 \},\u8232 \{\u8232 "no": 10,\u8232 "mark": "Yes",\u8232 "evidence": "It is only after these questions are addressed and one or the other conditions as enumerated above is satisfied, the power of arrest needs to be exercised.",\u8232 "reason": "It states that arrest requires consideration of necessity and satisfaction of specified Section 41 conditions rather than automatic arrest.",\u8232 "confidence": "high"\u8232 \},\u8232 \{\u8232 "no": 11,\u8232 "mark": "Yes",\u8232 "evidence": "cannot be arrested by the police officer only on his satisfaction that such person had committed the offence.",\u8232 "reason": "It directly states that merely believing the accused committed the offence is insufficient and additional necessity for arrest is required.",\u8232 "confidence": "high"\u8232 \},\u8232 \{\u8232 "no": 12,\u8232 "mark": "Yes",\u8232 "evidence": "not to automatically arrest when a case under Section 498-A of the IPC is registered but to satisfy themselves about the necessity for arrest",\u8232 "reason": "It directly answers the question by prohibiting automatic arrest after 498A registration and requiring assessment of arrest necessity.",\u8232 "confidence": "high"\u8232 \},\u8232 \{\u8232 "no": 13,\u8232 "mark": "Yes",\u8232 "evidence": "not to automatically arrest when a case under Section 498-A of the IPC is registered but to satisfy themselves about the necessity for arrest",\u8232 "reason": "It expressly states that police must not automatically arrest after 498A registration and instead must assess necessity under Section 41.",\u8232 "confidence": "high"\u8232 \},\u8232 \{\u8232 "no": 14,\u8232 "mark": "Partly",\u8232 "evidence": "After registration of the case on 3.6.1999, the investigating officer recorded the statements of witnesses under Section 161 of the Code of Criminal Procedure.",\u8232 "reason": "It mentions a registered 498A case and subsequent proceedings but does not state the governing rule against automatic arrest.",\u8232 "confidence": "high"\u8232 \},\u8232 \{\u8232 "no": 15,\u8232 "mark": "No",\u8232 "evidence": "Consequences of cruelty which are likely to drive a woman to commit suicide or to cause grave injury or danger to life, limb or health",\u8232 "reason": "It addresses the substantive elements of cruelty under Section 498A, not whether police may automatically arrest after registration.",\u8232 "confidence": "high"\u8232 \},\u8232 \{\u8232 "no": 16,\u8232 "mark": "No",\u8232 "evidence": "all these provisions relate to cognizance of the offence by the court.",\u8232 "reason": "It concerns court cognizance and Section 498A procedure, not the legality or necessity of automatic police arrest.",\u8232 "confidence": "high"\u8232 \}\u8232 ],\u8232 "good_answer_present": "Yes",\u8232 "best_passage_no": 12,\u8232 "caveats": ""\u8232 \}\
